      "created_at": "2019-12-27T09:50:22Z",
      "updated_at": "2019-12-27T09:50:22Z",
      "body": "I like the idea of improving the description. It will probably help in many cases, although in many cases people skim and won't see it. Better than nothing though!\r\n\r\n_Affiliation is your own organisation. That means you are an employee or otherwise working for the organisation. The affiliation request is sent to support@peeringdb.com if no one is affiliated to the organisation yet. Otherwise, the admins are contacted. Only affiliate once per organisation. If you don't get an answer within a couple of days, please contact support@peeringdb.com_\r\n\r\nChanges:\r\n* `s/Affilition/Affiliation/`\r\n* `s/ for //`\r\n* `s/employer/employee/`\r\n\r\nI appreciate the idea of letting requestors know the administrators, but are there any confidentiality  concerns there? I may not want unauthorized people knowing who my administrators are. Maybe instead we could change the final sentence to something like, _If you don't get an answer within a couple of days, or if the admins are no longer able to help, please contact support@peeringdb.com_",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
